{"predicates_before_run":["All short, unwrapped panels use exact signed integer paths. For each pointer value its probability at the prefix equals its full terminal mass. At each terminal cell the sum of the two signed branch amplitudes equals the blank-pointer amplitude.","The passive route log marginalizes to the original untagged squared law; a nonzero change in its unconditioned endpoint law after a physical copy also excludes every passive logging of the same terminal marginals.","The one-step singleton panel preserves unconditioned terminal marginals. The four-step singleton changes them. Resolving site at a two-site window and resolving rails in the singleton can change the full joint law. The rightmost path, parity-dark, and full windows have masses 1/64,0,1.","Compare the Fourier implementation with full signed exact vectors before longer trials. Retain every postflight conditional tail, including large errors; enforce norm checks but no empirical monotonicity threshold."],"exact_convention":"bit order 0=outside,1=inside. Each vector uses every site in [-bound,bound] in increasing order, R then L. For prefix_raw, bound=T. No omitted zeros. Square raw_by_tag entries and divide by denominator to recover the joint terminal law; the site-dephased numerators already contain squares. Passive values are rational probabilities.","physics":"Sharp (0,R), no field. Fourier convention exp(-ikx). Units epsilon=delta, pitch=delta\u00b2, tick=delta\u00b3; target p0=1. Window |x/T-delta*p0|<=delta^(11/10); T=round(delta^(-14/5)), S=round(delta^(-3)), observed at absolute tick T+S. Physical displacement starts at the nominal release center. The tolerance in velocity is 1/2. The reference acceptance 2w/pi is asymptotic.","instrument":"Extended complete detector law f(D)=D\u00b2 applies to (bit,x,rail) and terminal resolution is additive. The XOR copies membership of the site in W and preserves rail/site coherence within each class; there is no repeated measurement during eit